  "slug": "000-100-7630",
  "summary": "Agentic and benchmark tooling now encodes domain structure into auditable workflows spanning drug screening, gene-level evidence, and protein design.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is software that encodes domain structure into reproducible, auditable workflows rather than a single sequence-inference method. Fármaco orchestrates scalable drug-screening workflows over a provenance-tracked molecule memory, benchmarked on 22 tasks. GLESKit links gene-level databases, tools and literature into retained workspaces that yield reviewable reports, evaluated on GeneReportBench. LPT constrains LLM agent loops to a fixed orchestration backed by a curated ~14000-paper literature database for de novo protein binder design. BioResearchBench supplies a 50-task benchmark of expert-written research questions for evaluating frontier models. What is new is bounded, provenance-aware orchestration of LLM agents. Performance claims should be read against each paper's own benchmarks, since task domains differ.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-04"
}
